diff --git a/MATRIX_BRIDGE.md b/MATRIX_BRIDGE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bbf2dbe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/MATRIX_BRIDGE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Matrix Games shared-session staging
+
+This fork adds a private external-vehicle relay to AssettoServer. It is not yet
+a playable or production-validated native/browser crossplay release.
+
+Native players continue through AssettoServer's normal Steam authentication and
+checksum checks. Browser identity remains the responsibility of Matrix City's
+existing authenticated room admission. No browser connects to this relay directly.
+
+Set `MATRIX_ASSETTO_BRIDGE_CONFIG` to a private JSON file with `room`, `revision`,
+`tokenFile`, and a bounded `slots` array. Without this setting the relay is disabled.
+The token file must contain a high-entropy, 32-byte-or-longer random token and be
+readable only by the dedicated service user. Never commit it or put it in a URL.
+All reserved entry slots must use `AI=none`; keep `EnableAi: false` because Matrix
+City will own shared traffic. Native players, including administrators, cannot
+claim reserved slots. The entry list fixes each slot's model.
+
+The trusted relay posts a complete frame to `/_matrix/bridge/v1/exchange` using a
+Bearer header. The route only accepts loopback callers. For another machine use
+a private connection terminating on loopback; do not weaken the address check or
+publish the bridge route through a generic reverse proxy. JSON is limited to
+128 KiB. Frames are world/revision-bound, sequenced, time-bounded and rate-limited.
+A second stream cannot replace an active lease. Invalid frames do not renew it.
+External cars disappear after a three-second lease expiry.
+
+Poses are applied on the server update loop. Replies contain only native slot,
+model and pose data with generic driver names; no Steam IDs, IP addresses,
+account metadata, chat or credentials. This protocol does not create synthetic
+Steam users. Reserved cars participate in native connection/list/position packets.
+
+Before release, verify actual native-client visibility, reconnect and expiry;
+calibrate model-specific origin offsets and slopes; integrate the authenticated
+browser room and renderer; verify the complete approved fleet; and test traffic
+identity/capacity and collisions with both clients. Unit tests are not evidence
+of gameplay parity. Do not advertise either native/browser join target as ready
+until those checks pass.
+
+Scriban is updated from 6.6.0 to 7.6.1 to address the dependency advisories reported
+by restore. Preserve the upstream AGPL license, notices and corresponding source
+availability when this modified server is offered over a network.
